      "round": 1,
      "round_summary": "Round 1: Fix register read-after-write timing bug in initialization block. error_type=dut_bug, target_assertion_label=current_position_visited_after_init. Root cause: within when(!initDone), posReg (a Reg) is assigned via Mux and then immediately read as visited(posReg) index — Chisel register semantics return the OLD value (0) instead of the newly computed value, causing visited(0) to be set instead of visited(io.start). Fix: extract the initial-position computation into a combinational Wire (initPos) and use it for both posReg assignment and visited indexing, avoiding the register read-after-write pitfall. This also resolves the liveness property progress_when_unvisited_dest because with correct visited[] initialization the circuit state is consistent. No homologous assertions found — the other assertions (posReg_in_range, dest_in_range, visited_count_non_decreasing, progress_when_unvisited_dest) are structurally different.",
